# Private — never commit.
#
# interview-pacer's planning half lives here alongside the code as of 2026-07-28. It used to
# sit in a second directory in the private repo, which caused a real failure: /site-review ran
# from this directory on 2026-04-02, found no PROJECT_GOALS.md because it was in the other
# copy, and graded the app against goals inferred from the README instead.
#
# These are untracked and must stay that way. Note that .gitignore does NOT protect a file git
# already tracks, so never `git add -f` one of these. See ../LOCAL-ONLY-ENFORCEMENT.md.
interview-pacer/feedback/
interview-pacer/PROJECT_GOALS.md
interview-pacer/ROADMAP.md
interview-pacer/ui-playgrounds/

